WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.680
Fission throws out fast neutrons.

2
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:07.470
But uranium-235 captures
slow ones far more readily.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.810
So a reactor must slow its neutrons down,

4
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.180
and it does so with a moderator.

5
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:17.550
In the moderator, the neutron
loses speed by bouncing off nuclei,

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.460
like a ball on a snooker table.

7
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:23.240
Heavy nuclei, light nuclei,
something in between.

8
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.380
Which would slow the neutron down fastest?

9
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:30.770
In this mission, you'll work out how
control rods let operators turn a reactor's

10
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.770
power up or down.

11
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.760
Then you'll follow spent
fuel out of the reactor,

12
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:40.090
and see how waste is sorted
and stored by how active it is.

13
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: find out which nuclei
would slow a neutron down fastest.
